# The production web build's settings (`vite build`; `build:e2e` and `vite dev` use other modes and
# never read this file). apps/web/.env.example says what each one is.
#
# EVERY VALUE HERE IS PUBLIC. Vite compiles VITE_ values into the bundle every visitor downloads, the
# two hosts are already in the CSP (vercel.json, public/_headers), and a Supabase publishable key is
# made to ship to browsers. Never put SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY, DATABASE_URL, CODE_PEPPER or anything else
# from apps/server/.env here: env-production.test.ts fails on any key but these four, and on a
# secret-shaped value.
#
# A variable already set where the build runs wins over this file (Vite never overwrites one), so a
# host may still set them; nothing has to. promote-production.yml builds production from this file,
# and apps/web/scripts/check-production-bundle.mjs refuses a bundle missing any of them.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://exmjdaswedxhnzmpzqrq.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_tNmTI9vMGC9_YCiubVtFDw_A2e50TTx
VITE_SERVER_HTTP_URL=https://jackioh-server.onrender.com
VITE_SERVER_WS_URL=wss://jackioh-server.onrender.com/ws/match
